---

## Threats considered

- **T1 — Exported callable decoys:** If global, becomes dlsym gadget surface. Mitigation: keep file-local `static void` with fixed names `__oo_meta_decoy_<seq>`. Status: mitigated.
- **T2 — Main/ctor collision:** Name collision with entry points or init_array. Mitigation: fixed decimal sequence, no attributes/sections. Status: mitigated.
- **T3 — Function pointer tables:** Creating indirect call targets. Mitigation: hard ban on function pointers in decoys; `used,noinline` only. Status: mitigated.
- **T4 — system/exec sinks:** Planting shell gadgets in padding. Mitigation: volatile unsigned store + return only, no libc/process APIs. Status: mitigated.
- **T5 — Format-string / injection:** Source strings into decoy text. Mitigation: integer sequence only, clamped >= 0, no printf/scanf. Status: mitigated.
- **T6 — Opt-in marker footgun:** Silent layout change. Mitigation: line-start match, default off, residual free-names. Status: accepted policy residual.
- **T7 — Dead-code elimination:** Optimizers stripping decoys. Mitigation: emit `__attribute__((used,noinline))` under GNUC/clang. Status: mitigated.
- **T8 — Residual ROP into decoy bytes:** Controlled PC into padding. Mitigation: minimal instructions, no syscalls. Status: residual inherent to .text.
- **T9 — Overclaim vs CFI/ASLR:** Marketing path-A as runtime immune system. Mitigation: explicit residual wording — weak layout helper only, not CFI. Status: documented residual.
- **T10 — meta_epoch entropy:** Weak seed or leak. Mitigation: getentropy + fallback, not claimed CSPRNG, does not drive layout today. Status: honest floor.
- **T11 — Residual free-name bypass:** Full metamorphic codegen APIs. Mitigation: check_residual default-denies at check. Status: mitigated refuse.
- **T12 — Emit pipeline staleness:** Source/host binary lag. Mitigation: smoke soft-skips when binary lags, rebuild required. Status: process residual.

---

## OWN fix applied

**File:** `ooda/oodac/c_emit_meta.oo` only.
- Security contract block in file header pinning invariants.
- `static` retained; `used,noinline` under GNUC/clang.
- Comment block on each decoy: not main, not CFI, no fptrs/exec/fmt.
- idx clamp `< 0 → 0` + empty-id guard.
- `volatile unsigned int` pad only (no sinks, no format, no indirect calls).
- Preserved `c_meta_layout_emit_decoys(mode)`.

---

